{"event": "llm_start", "tag": "write", "prompt": "This PyTorch function is part of a model being trained. It is too slow to train with:\n\n```python\n@muse_kernel.fast\ndef gated_delta(q, k, v, g, beta, scale):\n    B, H, T, K = q.shape\n    S = q.new_zeros(B, H, K, v.shape[-1]).float()\n    outs = []\n    for t in range(T):\n        S = S * g[:, :, t].float().exp()[..., None, None]\n        kt = k[:, :, t].float()\n        pred = (S * kt[..., None]).sum(-2)\n        S = S + (beta[:, :, t].float()[..., None] * (v[:, :, t].float() - pred))[..., None, :] * kt[..., None]\n        outs.append((S * (q[:, :, t].float() * scale)[..., None]).sum(-2))\n    return torch.stack(outs, dim=2)\n\n```\n\nThe model calls it like this (shapes, dtypes and strides as observed):\n\n    muse_jobs.j_55f24fcd745cb06e.gated_delta(Tensor(shape=[2, 4, 512, 128], dtype=bfloat16, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 4, 512, 128], dtype=bfloat16, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 4, 512, 128], dtype=bfloat16, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 4, 512], dtype=float32, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 4, 512], dtype=float32, contiguous), 0.08838834764831845)\n\nObserved on every call:\n- k has unit-norm rows (L2 over the last dimension)\n- g is <= 0 (a log decay)\n- beta lies in [0, 1]\n\nIt takes 111 ms forward on this call on an NVIDIA L4. Write a fast Triton implementation for the L4\n(Ada, sm_89, Triton 3.5).\n\nRequirements:\n- Define `def kernel_function(q, k, v, g, beta, scale):` with the same arguments and semantics, returning the same result.\n- It must match the function on any inputs it accepts within the observed constraints.\n- The computation must happen in your own @triton.jit kernels; the Python wrapper may only allocate, reshape,\n  launch and do cheap elementwise prep. Do not import or copy any existing implementation.\n\nYou cannot run anything. Return the complete module in one ```python block, then 2-4 sentences on your\napproach and anything you are unsure about.", "t": 1793080038.5501432}
